            "content": "<h3><strong>Labyrinths</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; a winding spiral path leading to a central area</p>\n<p><strong>Labyrinths compared with mazes</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Mazes are a type of <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_31\">______</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_32\">______</span> is needed to navigate through a maze</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; the word &lsquo;maze&rsquo; is derived from a word meaning a feeling of <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_33\">______</span></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Labyrinths represent a journey through life</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; they have frequently been used in <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_34\">______</span> and prayer</p>\n<p><strong>Early examples of the labyrinth spiral</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Ancient carvings on <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_35\">______</span> have been found across many cultures</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; The Pima, a Native American tribe, wove the symbol on baskets</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Ancient Greeks used the symbol on <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_36\">______</span></p>\n<p><strong>Walking labyrinths</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; The largest surviving example of a turf labyrinth once had a big <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_37\">______</span> at its centre</p>\n<p><strong>Labyrinths nowadays</strong></p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Believed to have a beneficial impact on mental and physical health, e.g., walking a maze can reduce a person&rsquo;s <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_38\">______</span> rate</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Used in medical and health and fitness settings and also prisons</p>\n<p>●&nbsp;&nbsp; Popular with patients, visitors and staff in hospitals</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; patients who can&rsquo;t walk can use &lsquo;finger labyrinths&rsquo; made from <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_39\">______</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &ndash;&nbsp; research has shown that Alzheimer&rsquo;s sufferers experience less <span class=\"gap-placeholder\" data-question-id=\"gf_40\">______</span></p>",
